            <ArticleTitle>Stent thrombosis in a patient receiving chemotherapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>383-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intravascular stents are successfully used during coronary revascularization. Subacute stent thrombosis is a rare complication, associated with a 40-60% risk of myocardial infarction, and occurs 5-10 days after implantation. We describe a case of late stent thrombosis potentially due to delayed endothelialization from cancer chemotherapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
